div.p:
Your Excellency: I have had the honor to receive
                    your dispatch of the 13th instant, stating that you are in receipt of a report
                    from the acting consul-general at Shanghai, to the following effect:

In a word, the plain language of each article of each treaty must stand for law;
                    and as your excellency adverted to the treatment accorded to Chinese in the
                    United States, it seemed best to make the comment given above.
